37:Autism spectrum disorder (ASD) is a neurodevelopmental condition characterized by a wide range of behavioral phenotypes,  including  persistent  deficits  in  social  communication  and  interaction,  repetitive  behaviors,  and restricted  interests  [1].  Over  the  past  several  decades, convergent evidence of impairment in social information processing  has  indicated  that  ASD  is  a  socio-cognitive condition  [2].  Recent  studies  have  demonstrated  that sensory processing may be central to understanding the neurobiology of ASD [3]. As such, a remaining challenge in ASD research is to identify the common neurobiological basis underlying its system-wide effects.
